snippet.textDisplay:
@brrrrrrennan AI is just that… artificial. Meaning, we’re still going to need humans to develop new medicine, new techniques, and medicine requires a human doctor to be present. 

So, yes.. we may have fully automated surgeries in the future but that’s also not a bad a thing. An AI controlled robot is far less prone to error in surgery than a human. 

But it will never be fully automated. There will always be doctors and nurses in that room.

