@Chrisistheone1 I can actually answer those question.

It is a Basic Income, so if they set the amount at $1,000 dollars a month, everyone who is an adult US citizen would receive $1,000 every month to supplement their income, so that no one is making less than $1,000 a month regardless of their employment status. 

Legislators would decide the actual amount received. The market would still decide who gets to drive the nicer car. That wouldn't change.

