snippet.textDisplay:
@u@unicornkisses7359 didn't even know what a myotherapist was and had to resort to search. Interesting my spell checker underlines it in red so I don't feel so bad. I am sure your job is safe. Look robots can't drive cars reliably yet beyond highly controlled situations. 

You would think relative to most peoples jobs that driving cars requires fairly low levels of intelligence, manual dexterity, human interaction, physical strength etc yet look how much money and tech is being poured into that one thing. The best we have is Waymo with incredibly expensive vehicles that only drive in a few parts of a few cities, still require humans to help drive and service them et al.

Yes Amazon will reduce the numbers of people it needs but yes it will still need people. We need to think more about ensuring meaningful occupations for those displaced for the good of us all, not a few billionaires. And perhaps many need a better work life balance today too.

